{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1365245-hobgoblins-and-other-splats","id":1365245,"title":"Hobgoblins and other splats.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-04T07:10:32-08:00","id":1365245,"title":"Hobgoblins and other splats.","content":"Is it possible for another supernatural being turn into a Hobgoblin or Goblin Queen?<br /> <br /> After reading the Hedge Denizen condition I got caught thinking on the following statement:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\">If the character was mortal, or <u>another non-</u></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><u>changeling</u> unlucky enough to fall in with hob</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">-</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">goblins, she immediately learns three Goblin Con</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">tracts of the player\u2019s choice. If she is a Storyteller </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">character, the Storyteller may substitute <u>Dread </u></span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><u>Powers</u> for any of these </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">(p. 253)</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">. She can switch </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">them out each dawn as above.</span></span><br /> <br /> Do you guys think is it possible for a<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Werewolf or Vampire to turn into a Goblin Queen?</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T07:51:52-08:00","id":1365253,"title":"","content":"Absolutely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T08:13:44-08:00","id":1365259,"title":"","content":"That's interesting. I wonder what would happen if the hobgoblin fell in love with them back?<br /> <br /> Where did you read this? And what's a Goblin Queen? (Idk that much about Changeling: the Lost.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T11:29:48-08:00","id":1365307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1365245-hobgoblins-and-other-splats?p=1365259#post1365259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interesting. I wonder what would happen if the hobgoblin fell in love with them back?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://lmgtfy.com/?q=fall+in+with+meaning\" target=\"_blank\">Not &quot;fall in love with hobgoblins.&quot;</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where did you read this? </div> </div> </div>The Hedge Denizen Condition in the Changeling: the Lost 2e core rulebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what's a Goblin Queen? (Idk that much about Changeling: the Lost.) </div> </div> </div>Accruing a sufficient degree of Goblin Debt from using Goblin Contracts or taking deals from hobgoblins gives you the Hedge Denizen Condition, which warps your mien, removes your affinity cost-breaks for Arcadian Contracts, stops you from learning new Court Contracts, turns off the benefits of your Mantle, makes Clarity damage rolls a little more dangerous, gives you the Deprived Condition if you go to Earth until you come back, and prevents the Storyteller from getting rid of points of your Goblin Debt by spending it to make things harder or weirder for your character.<br /> <br /> In exchange, you can use Goblin Contracts without incurring Goblin Debt, you can make deals and sell Contracts like a regular hobgoblin (collecting Debt in the process), and you can change what Goblin Contracts you know (though the number of them remains the same and buying new ones costs the same amount) whenever the sun rises over the Hedge<br /> <br /> You can work off points of your Goblin Debt by doing favors for the goblin you got your Contracts or favors from (and doing so gives you Beats from this Persistent Condition), and if you've gotten your Goblin Debt below the point where you became a Hedge Denizen and then heal a point of Clarity (or gain or lose a dot of Integrity-or-an-equivalent-trait) then you can return to being the thing that you were, albeit still having any Goblin Contracts you knew and still having as much Goblin Debt as you worked your way down to.<br /> <br /> If you have Touchstones, and you lose one while you're a Hedge Denizen and then lose Clarity-or-an-equivalent-trait, you can become a Goblin Queen, which doesn't grant your Wyrd as a bonus to attempts to track you down, has a number of loyal goblin Retainers (Merit dots equal to your Wyrd, distributed as you like to the usual limit of five per Retainer), and gets four dots of Status (Goblins) along with immediate knowledge of the assumed names and titles of any creatures in the local Hedge that outrank you, plus all the other benefits and drawbacks of being a Hedge Denizen.<br /> <br /> In exchange, you can't use your Court Contracts, you can't leave the Hedge without wrapping pieces of it around you as a mantle to let you visit Arcadia or the mortal world for a few hours per day, you can't integrate your Icons by leaving the Hedge with them, and Clarity damage rolls get even riskier.<br /> <br /> You get Beats from collecting Goblin Debt as a Goblin Queen, but the only ways to get rid of the Goblin Queen Condition are to work off five points of Goblin Debt (dropping back down to Hedge Denizen) or find a mortal child to take your place (restoring you immediately and triggering a Clarity attack or breaking point along with putting a child who remembers you abandoned them in a seat of power).<br /> <br /> It's a really neat part of 2e that I'm hoping the supplements will cover in more detail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T12:14:00-08:00","id":1365321,"title":"","content":"Ohhhhh ok<br /> <br /> Thanks. I might check it out when the Hedge book comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}